//! check: fail(E0206)
//! phase: lex
//! conforms: gram.type.start, gram.type
//!
//! s163 (wolf-lang#320) — a keyword where a type must begin is E0206,
//! "expected a type", at the keyword. `proc` is a keyword (it spells
//! `spawn proc`), not a type, so the parameter's type position holds a
//! token that cannot begin one. The compiler has answered E0206 since
//! about bs12 and no corpus file pinned it, so an implementation
//! reading only the spec and the corpus had nothing to transcribe
//! (lupin once spent the number on an invention of its own). Both
//! machines answer E0206 at the `proc` since lupin 0.1.32's is45.

fn f(p: proc) {
}

fn main() -> !int {
    0
}
